Z||000000||filthyscarecrow||10-07-2001||08:20 PM||||okay, for those of you who have removed the stone age v-6 from the car, anyone ever weighed the engine/gearbox?i'm wondering on the weight of both the v6/4spd gearbox, and the 4 cyl/4spd gearbox. anyone? anyone? thanks guys...||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||10-07-2001||08:26 PM||||I've had both 4 speeds side-by-side and they are almost identical. The V6 has some extra webbing on the case, but besides that they have the same dimensions. The size of the internals (gears) should have very little effect on weight. The Getrag is quite a bit heavier than a four speed, I realized this when unloading them from my truck, but I have never put them on a scale to see just how much of a difference there is.||||reg||1
Z||000002||filthyscarecrow||10-07-2001||08:51 PM||||actually i'm lookin for the package weight. i'm considering several engine swaps adn i wanna know what my weight distribution will be compared to stock. i don't care whether they're the same, i wanna know how much the engine and gearbox weigh together. anyone? <p>[This message has been edited by filthyscarecrow (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan87GT||10-07-2001||08:54 PM||||Both V6 and 4cyl 4sp trannies are the same, I have a 4sp out of a 4cyl cavalier in my 86SE. Different gear ratio's depending on the year. The Getrag is a 5sp.||||reg||1
